{"500":{"assignees":[],"author":"ink999107","base":"main","body":"## Summary\n\nTurns the transcript into a live run view and lets a finished run be read back:\n\n- **Permissions** — a run that stops for approval renders a card with the pending request, so the decision is made in the conversation rather than in a side channel.\n- **Tool cards** — each tool call shows its input, output and status, and a nested substream for tools that run other tools.\n- **Run folding** — completed steps fold into a summary row, keeping a long run readable while every step stays one click away.\n- **Replay** — a finished turn is reconstructed from the persisted run records (`foldRunRecords`, `replayRun`, `RunReplay`, `placeReplays`), so reopening a session shows the same steps, tool output and permission decisions.\n- **Reducer and stream** — permission state, tool traces and replay cursors are folded into the existing run state.\n\n## Stack\n\nPart **2 of 6**, built on #499. The PR is cumulative on `main`; the incremental change is the [compare against the previous branch](https://github.com/ink999107/sciencediscovery/compare/pr/01-foundation...pr/02-run-stream).\n\n## Testing\n\n- `pnpm --filter @sciencediscovery/desktop typecheck` — pass\n- `pnpm --filter @sciencediscovery/desktop test` — 137 passed\n- The full `ci:l1` / `ci:ut` / `ci:st` layers were run on the tip of the stack\n\n## Merge order\n\nThis is PR 2 of 6 and the branches are stacked. Merge bottom-up with a merge or rebase (not squash) so the next PR collapses to its own commit, then move that branch onto the new `main` before merging it.\n","ci":{"checks":[{"conclusion":"success","name":"Select CI policy","url":"https://github.com/openJiuwen-ai/sciencediscovery/actions/runs/39893171730/job/120217401480"},{"conclusion":"success","name":"L1 (static checks)","url":"https://github.com/openJiuwen-ai/sciencediscovery/actions/runs/39893171730/job/120217474012"},{"conclusion":"skipped","name":"L4/L5 real E2E","url":"https://gi