base":"main","body":"## Summary\n\nAdds the third column: a workspace panel over the session's files.\n\n- **File tree** — the session's file listing, with previews opened as tabs and the tree state kept per session.\n- **Previews** — text and image files render inline; molecular structures open in a Mol* viewer loaded as its own chunk, so the main bundle does not carry the renderer.\n- **Resize** — the splitter between the conversation and the panel drives `--panel-width`; the column and the panel read the same value, so they cannot disagree, and the width is remembered.\n- **Uploads** — files can be dropped on the panel or chosen from the composer; uploads go through the session API and refresh the tree.\n- **Session files** — the client gains the listing and upload calls the panel and previews use.\n\n## Stack\n\nPart **3 of 6**, built on #500. The PR is cumulative on `main`; the incremental change is the [compare against the previous branch](https://github.com/ink999107/sciencediscovery/compare/pr/02-run-stream...pr/03-workspace-panel).\n\n## Testing\n\n- `pnpm --filter @sciencediscovery/desktop typecheck` — pass\n- `pnpm --filter @sciencediscovery/desktop test` — 197 passed\n- The full `ci:l1` / `ci:ut` / `ci:st` layers were run on the tip of the stack\n\n## Merge order\n\nThis is PR 3 of 6 and the branches are stacked. Merge bottom-up with a merge or rebase (not squash) so the next PR collapses to its own commit, then move that branch onto the new `main` before merging it.\n","ci":{"checks":[{"conclusion":"success","name":"Select CI policy","url":"https://github.com/openJiuwen-ai/sciencediscovery/actions/runs/39893230929/job/120217595883"},{"conclusion":"success","name":"L1 (static checks)","url":"https://github.com/openJiuwen-ai/sciencediscovery/actions/runs/39893230929/job/120217656613"},{"conclusion":"skipped","name":"L4/L5 real E2E","url":"https://github.com/openJiuwen-ai/sciencediscovery/actions/runs/39893230929/job/120217658470"},{"conclusion":"success",